WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.620
A king carved his regret into

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.390
stone. It is still there.

3
00:00:06.008 --> 00:00:08.268
Rock Edict thirteen, as

4
00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:09.648
translated by E.

5
00:00:09.648 --> 00:00:12.308
Hultzsch. The king calls himself

6
00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:14.208
Devanampriya Priyadarshi;

7
00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:16.448
historians identify him as

8
00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:17.438
Ashoka.

9
00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:20.078
Eight years after his crowning,

10
00:00:20.078 --> 00:00:22.118
he conquered Kalinga, on the

11
00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:23.338
eastern coast.

12
00:00:23.338 --> 00:00:24.978
The edict says:

13
00:00:24.978 --> 00:00:26.338
a hundred and fifty thousand

14
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:28.458
deported, a hundred thousand

15
00:00:28.458 --> 00:00:30.818
slain, and many times as many

16
00:00:30.818 --> 00:00:31.618
dead.

17
00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:34.582
Then the king looks at the cost.

18
00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:36.482
In his own word, it is

19
00:00:36.482 --> 00:00:37.452
repentance.

20
00:00:38.336 --> 00:00:40.296
Even a hundredth part of that

21
00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:42.696
suffering, he says, would now be

22
00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:44.786
deeply painful to him.

23
00:00:45.118 --> 00:00:46.778
So he turns to dhamma:

24
00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:49.538
the study of morality, the love

25
00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:51.938
of morality, and teaching it to

26
00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:54.018
others. He calls this the

27
00:00:54.018 --> 00:00:55.548
principal conquest.

28
00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.262
He does not give up his power.

29
00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:00.642
The edict warns the forest

30
00:01:00.642 --> 00:01:02.722
peoples that he can still punish

31
00:01:02.722 --> 00:01:05.142
them, so that they feel ashamed,

32
00:01:05.142 --> 00:01:07.112
and are not killed.

33
00:01:07.878 --> 00:01:10.018
He says this conquest has been

34
00:01:10.018 --> 00:01:11.938
won as far as the Yona king

35
00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.418
Antiyoka, and south to the

36
00:01:14.418 --> 00:01:16.368
Cholas and Pandyas.

37
00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:17.704
For GS1:

38
00:01:17.704 --> 00:01:20.417
the Kalinga war, Rock Edict

39
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:22.627
thirteen, and dhamma.

40
00:01:23.437 --> 00:01:24.224
For GS4:

41
00:01:24.224 --> 00:01:26.617
a ruler's own words on what

42
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:27.627
power costs.

43
00:01:28.932 --> 00:01:32.612
A king, a rock, and a sentence

44
00:01:32.612 --> 00:01:34.742
he did not have to write.
